  "_approach": "Two-bar reload build on a 32nd grid, kick kept relentless 4/4 the whole way (speed garage rarely loses the floor): the snare enters in 16ths at beat 3 of bar 1, and in bar 2 climbs through 16ths into 32nds with velocity ramping so the four loudest hits (124-127) sit on the very last 32nds, straight into the drop. Ref: Double 99 'Ripgroove', Tuff Jam era rewind sections. (re-voiced for the Vermona DRM1 MKIII's 8 channels)",
